{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113763","id":3082768681,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc63v1Ep","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113763/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113763/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113763/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/126655e307e7d3166d784360689d07a7967fc72b","number":113763,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add FXAA support to the Compatibility renderer","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This adds FXAA support to the Compatibility renderer, making it have parity with Godot 3.x GLES3/GLES2 on this aspect.\r\n\r\nWhen attempting to use SMAA in Compatibility (which isn't currently implemented), it will now fall back to FXAA to provide an experience as close as possible.\r\n\r\nSMAA support could be added in a future PR (OpenGL ES 3.0 and WebGL 2.0 can support it), but it's more involved.\r\n\r\n- This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/69463.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_screen_space_aa.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24039744/test_screen_space_aa.zip)\r\n\r\n## Preview\r\n\r\n### No glow, no SSAO\r\n\r\n*The first image has the separate tonemap pass disabled, as we don't use any effect that requires it (and `scaling_3d_scale` is `1.0`). There is a slight color shift as soon as the separate tonemap pass kicks in, but this also happens in `master` with no FXAA.*\r\n\r\nDisabled | FXAA\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195625\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b0e6476f-1562-4f9a-a793-2b8a8243c4ed\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195630\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f92a6e3-ed9d-4da9-ace3-6ff0ff5e2461\" />\r\n\r\n### Glow + SSAO\r\n\r\nDisabled | FXAA\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195601\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6188e32c-cdfd-4d80-81aa-2cb6041bf1b4\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195606\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0a90f7d-b847-4e6f-98d1-9c36ec9aab55\" />\r\n\r\n### Glow + SSAO + AgX tonemapping\r\n\r\nDisabled | FXAA\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195734\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5e08fe32-945c-4d74-8140-6c7399059933\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Screenshot_20251208_195739\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6c69fb4-d94b-4c52-b3e8-2d1c845831c2\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## TODO\r\n\r\n- [x] Check order of operations (should FXAA be before or after tonemapping and/or glow)?\r\n  - Currently, FXAA still works when glow is enabled, but it's less effective overall.\r\n  - https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3628687220\r\n- [x] Check if the luminance exposure multiplier is correctly applied. It's possible that I got it wrong, or that I'm doing the operation for no benefit.\r\n  - https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113763#issuecomment-3628687220","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}",